```json
// GET /reports/jobs/9931 — running
{ "jobId": "9931", "state": "running", "progress": 0.62, "resultUrl": null }

// GET /reports/jobs/9931 — done
{ "jobId": "9931", "state": "done", "progress": 1.0, "resultUrl": "/reports/9931/download" }

// GET /reports/jobs/9931 — failed
{
  "jobId": "9931",
  "state": "failed",
  "progress": 0.4,
  "resultUrl": null,
  "error": { "code": "SOURCE_FILE_CORRUPT", "message": "Input file could not be parsed" }
}
```

One shape, three states — the client checks `state` first, and only reads `resultUrl`/`error` once it knows which branch it's in. `progress` stays present even on failure, showing how far it got before something went wrong.
